* ============================================================================
*  OCSW_beh.lib  --  Behavioral LTspice model of a generic overcurrent switch
*                    (an ideal-ish power switch with a definite-time
*                    overcurrent trip: the hard-short part of an eFuse,
*                    without its I2t curve)
*
*  Status    : generic, vendor-independent model for power-distribution and
*              protection-coordination studies. The switch opens when its
*              current stays above IMAX for at least TOC seconds; it stays
*              open (latched) until EN is taken low, or retries after TRETRY.
*              The defaults are engineering estimates flagged "[EST]" (see
*              README.md, part 7). Use the eFuse model (VNF1048F_beh.lib)
*              when the I2t curve, the gate drive or the FET matter.
*  Simulator : LTspice (validated with LTspice 26.0.2; uses B-sources with
*              if() and boolean operators; no idt(), no table(), no
*              min()/max() in any feedback path)
*
*  Contents
*    OCSW        overcurrent switch (power path IN -> OUT, logic EN / FLT
*                referred to GND)                                      5 pins
*    OC_LATCH / OC_FIX  helper primitives (SR latch, fault-hook level)
*
*  What is modeled (and why it matters at system level)
*    * on-resistance RON and off-state leakage ROFF (drop, loss, leakage)
*    * current sense with a first-order filter TSNS (the detection delay of a
*      real comparator: what a fast short-circuit ramp overshoots by)
*    * definite-time overcurrent trip: a timer that runs while the sensed
*      current is above IMAX and restarts from zero when it drops below, so
*      only an overcurrent that lasts TOC without interruption trips
*      (inrush shorter than TOC passes; time grading between levels)
*    * latch-off with FLT output; reset by EN low, or auto-retry (hiccup)
*      after TRETRY
*    * active clamp VCLAMP across the switch (inductive turn-off: where the
*      energy of the harness and load inductance goes)
*    * one or both current directions (DIR) for the trip; the switch itself
*      conducts and blocks in both directions
*    * built-in fault hook for FMEA (stuck-on / stuck-off), inactive by
*      default
*  Not modeled on purpose: an I2t / thermal trip curve (use EFUSE48_MOD),
*  the switching transient (the switch changes state in one time step;
*  with inductance in the loop the clamp sets the current fall), current
*  limiting (the switch is either on or tripping), the FET's thermal
*  network and SOA, body diode, under-voltage lockout, gate drive and
*  charge pump, supply current of the controller, temperature dependence
*  of RON and IMAX.
*
*  Node voltages used as signals (probe with V(<inst>:<node>)), all referred
*  to the GND pin:
*      isf   filtered sensed current [A] (|I| for DIR = 0, I for DIR = 1)
*      oc    overcurrent comparator, 1 = isf > IMAX
*      tm    overcurrent timer [s] (1 V = 1 s): rises at 1 V/s while oc,
*            restarts from 0 when oc drops; trip at tm = TOC
*      lat   trip latch, 1 = tripped (= FLT / VLOG)
*      tr    retry timer [s] (1 V = 1 s), runs while latched if TRETRY > 0
*      s     switch command, 1 = closed, 0 = open
*      pd    power dissipated in the switch [W] (channel + clamp)
*  I(<inst>:Vs) is the switch current (> 0 from IN to OUT), clamp included.
* ============================================================================


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  OCSW  -- overcurrent switch
*
*  Pins: IN, OUT  power path (current > 0 from IN to OUT)
*        GND      reference of the logic and of the internal signals
*                 (no current flows into GND from the power path)
*        EN       enable input, high (> VLOG/2) = on; internal 100 kOhm
*                 pull-up to VLOG, so an unconnected EN means "always on".
*                 Taking EN low opens the switch and clears a trip.
*        FLT      fault output, VLOG through 100 Ohm when tripped, else 0 V
*
*  IN --[Vs]--+--[ g(s) = 1/ROFF + (1/RON - 1/ROFF) s ]--+-- OUT
*             +--[ active clamp: (|V| - VCLAMP)/RCL ]-----+
*
*  Parameters:
*    IMAX    10      overcurrent threshold [A]
*    TOC     1m      overcurrent time [s]: the switch opens when the current
*                    stays above IMAX for TOC without interruption
*                    (TOC = 0: as fast as the sense filter, see TSNS)
*    RON     1m      on-resistance [Ohm] [EST]
*    ROFF    10Meg   off-state resistance (leakage) [Ohm] [EST]
*    TSNS    100n    time constant of the current-sense filter [s] [EST]
*    TRST    0       restart time constant of the overcurrent timer [s]
*                    when the current drops below IMAX; 0 = TOC/100,
*                    at most 1 us
*    DIR     0       0: trip on |I| (both directions); 1: trip on I > IMAX
*                    only (IN -> OUT; a reverse current never trips)
*    TRETRY  0       0: latch until EN goes low; > 0: off time [s] after a
*                    trip, then the switch closes again (hiccup)
*    VCLAMP  80      active clamp voltage across the switch [V] (both
*                    polarities) [EST]; 0 = no clamp. Must be above the
*                    highest supply-to-load voltage in normal operation.
*    RCL     0.1     dynamic resistance of the clamp [Ohm] [EST]
*    VLOG    3.3     logic level of EN (threshold VLOG/2) and FLT [V]
*    FI_ID, FI_ID2, FID, FI_MODE, FI_MODE2, FI_T, FI_TTR
*                    built-in fault hook (FMEA simulation, README part 6):
*                    active when the scenario number FID equals FI_ID (mode
*                    FI_MODE) or FI_ID2 (mode FI_MODE2), from FI_T in FI_TTR:
*                      mode 1  stuck-on: the switch stays closed (RON)
*                              whatever the control does; FLT still reports
*                              the trip
*                      mode 2  stuck-off: the switch opens (ROFF)
*
*  Trip time for a current step from I0 to I1 (> IMAX) at t = 0:
*    t_trip = TSNS ln((I1 - I0)/(I1 - IMAX)) + TOC
*  (the switch then opens within one time step). For a current ramp dI/dt the sensed
*  current lags by ~TSNS, so the current at the trip is
*    I_trip ~ IMAX + dI/dt (TSNS + TOC)
*  and the peak current of a hard short is set by TOC and the loop
*  inductance, not by IMAX.
*
*  Analyses: .tran; .ac (the switch state is frozen at its DC value: RON
*  if EN is high, ROFF if low). In the DC operating point the switch is
*  closed if EN is high and the timers are 0; an overcurrent present at
*  t = 0 starts the timer at t = 0 (the latch cannot set in the DC solve).
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt OCSW IN OUT GND EN FLT
+ IMAX=10 TOC=1m RON=1m ROFF=10Meg TSNS=100n TRST=0 DIR=0
+ TRETRY=0 VCLAMP=80 RCL=0.1 VLOG=3.3
+ FI_ID=0 FI_ID2=0 FID=0 FI_MODE=1 FI_MODE2=1 FI_T=10m FI_TTR=1u

.param TOCE  = {max(TOC, 1n)}
.param TRSTE = {if(TRST>0, TRST, min(1u, TOCE/100))}
.param GON   = {1/RON}
.param GOFF  = {1/ROFF}
.param DIRF  = {if(DIR>0.5, 1, 0)}
.param RTA   = {if(TRETRY>0, 1, 0)}
.param TRE   = {if(TRETRY>0, TRETRY, 1e9)}
.param CLA   = {if(VCLAMP>0, 1, 0)}
.param VCLE  = {if(VCLAMP>0, VCLAMP, 1e6)}
*  fault hook: FIA1 = stuck-on active, FIA2 = stuck-off active
.param FIA  = {(FI_ID>0 & abs(FID-FI_ID)<0.5) | (FI_ID2>0 & abs(FID-FI_ID2)<0.5)}
.param FIM  = {if(FI_ID>0 & abs(FID-FI_ID)<0.5, FI_MODE, if(FI_ID2>0 & abs(FID-FI_ID2)<0.5, FI_MODE2, 0))}
.param FIA1 = {FIA*(FIM==1)}
.param FIA2 = {FIA*(FIM==2)}

* ---------------- power path -------------------------------------------------
*  Vs senses the total current. The channel conductance is 1/RON or 1/ROFF
*  by the switch command s; the fault hook moves the effective state to 1
*  (stuck-on) or 0 (stuck-off). The hook factors are constant parameters,
*  so an inactive hook has exactly zero derivatives (README part 6).
Vs  IN n1 0
Bsw n1 OUT I=V(n1,OUT)*({GOFF} + {GON-GOFF}*(V(s,GND)
+  + {FIA1}*V(fix,GND)*(1-V(s,GND)) - {FIA2}*V(fix,GND)*V(s,GND)))
*  active clamp: conducts (|V| - VCLAMP)/RCL above VCLAMP, in both
*  polarities; exactly zero (and zero derivatives) when VCLAMP = 0
Bcl n1 OUT I={CLA/RCL}*(V(n1,OUT) - limit(V(n1,OUT), -{VCLE}, {VCLE}))

* ---------------- enable and fault output ------------------------------------
Bvl vl GND V={VLOG}
Rpu vl EN 100k
Ben enl GND V=V(EN,GND)>{VLOG/2}
Bfo fo GND V={VLOG}*V(lat,GND)
Rfo fo FLT 100

* ---------------- current sense and overcurrent timer -------------------------
*  isf: sensed current through a first-order filter (TSNS)
Bis is GND V={DIRF}*I(Vs) + {1-DIRF}*abs(I(Vs))
Rsf is isf 1k
Csf isf GND {TSNS/1k}
Boc oc GND V=V(isf,GND)>{IMAX}
*  tm: one monotonic timer state [s] on a normalized 1 F capacitor (no
*  idt(), no feedback through a deglitch filter): rises at exactly 1 V/s
*  while oc, restarts with TRST when oc drops; 0 in the DC operating point
Ctm tm GND 1 Rpar=1T
Btm GND tm I=if(time<=0, -V(tm,GND)*1k,
+  if(V(oc,GND)>0.5, 1, -V(tm,GND)/{TRSTE}))
Bts ts GND V=V(tm,GND)>={TOCE}

* ---------------- trip latch, reset and retry ---------------------------------
*  reset: EN low, or the retry timer has run TRETRY while latched
Ctr tr GND 1 Rpar=1T
Btr GND tr I=if(time<=0, -V(tr,GND)*1k,
+  if(V(lat,GND)>0.5, {RTA}, -V(tr,GND)/{TRSTE}))
Brs rst GND V=(V(enl,GND)<0.5) | (V(tr,GND)>={TRE})
Xl ts rst lat GND OC_LATCH DCS=0

* ---------------- switch state ------------------------------------------------
*  s = 1 (closed) or 0 (open), a boolean of the logic: the switch changes
*  state within one time step. Deliberately no state variable: a dynamic
*  switch state (a ramp or lag of TSW ~ 1 us) stays coupled into the power
*  path through dI/ds = V(IN,OUT)/RON while it settles, and collapsed the
*  trapezoidal time step to ~10 ps in multi-instance netlists (README 7.9).
*  A boolean has zero derivative.
Bs s GND V=(V(enl,GND)>0.5) & (V(lat,GND)<0.5)

* ---------------- dissipation -------------------------------------------------
Bpd pd GND V=V(IN,OUT)*I(Vs)

* ---------------- built-in fault hook -----------------------------------------
Xfi fix GND OC_FIX ID={FI_ID} ID2={FI_ID2} FID={FID} TF={FI_T} TTR={FI_TTR}
.ends OCSW


* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Helper primitives (logic levels 0/1 V referred to local GND)
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  OC_FIX -- fault level of the built-in fault hook: 0 V, or 0 .. 1 V from
*  TF (in TTR) when the scenario number FID equals ID or ID2 (as FI_X of
*  models/FAULTS_beh.lib, which this library does not need). No breakpoint
*  source inside a device model (README, numerical guidance).
.subckt OC_FIX X GND ID=0 ID2=0 FID=0 TF=10m TTR=1u
.param ACT = {(ID>0 & abs(FID-ID)<0.5) | (ID2>0 & abs(FID-ID2)<0.5)}
Bx X GND V={ACT}*limit((time-{TF})/{TTR}, 0, 1)
Rx X GND 1G
.ends OC_FIX

*  Set-dominant SR latch (as EF_LATCH). Regenerative hold, Q snaps to 0 or 1
*  in ~10 ns; forced to reset in the DC operating point unless S is active.
*  DCS=0: S cannot set it in the DC operating point either (the trip removes
*  its own cause, so a fault at t = 0 would leave no consistent DC solution;
*  it latches at the first time step instead).
.subckt OC_LATCH S R Q GND DCS=1
Bl GND Q I=if(V(S,GND)>0.5 & (time>0 | {DCS}>0.5), 1-V(Q,GND),
+  if(V(R,GND)>0.5 | time<=0, -V(Q,GND), if(V(Q,GND)>0.5, 1-V(Q,GND), -V(Q,GND))))
Cl Q GND 10n
Rl Q GND 1T
.ends OC_LATCH
